WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.552
The applied challenge asks you to reshape the long sales table into one row per product.

00:00:04.552 --> 00:00:07.842
Create January, February, and March revenue columns.

00:00:07.842 --> 00:00:11.042
Preserve NULL when there is no observation for a product-month.

00:00:11.042 --> 00:00:14.387
Then explain why the result has fewer rows than the source.

00:00:14.387 --> 00:00:16.537
Do not start with syntax alone.

00:00:16.537 --> 00:00:20.382
First state the output grain and the measure that belongs in each pivot cell.

00:00:20.382 --> 00:00:25.242
Connect this idea to a machine-learning workflow converting wide measurements into tidy long data.

00:00:25.242 --> 00:00:29.772
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:29.772 --> 00:00:36.092
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:36.092 --> 00:00:40.667
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:45.520
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
